<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>CSuiteFinder — work email lookup API</title>
<meta name="description" content="Resolve a name and a company domain to a work email. Deliverability, enrichment, patterns and company data. <%= @trial_tokens %> free tokens to start.">
<style>
  :root {
    --bg: #fbfaf8;
    --surface: #ffffff;
    --border: #e4e0d9;
    --text: #1c1a17;
    --muted: #6b6560;
    --accent: #b8541f;
    --accent-soft: #fdf1e8;
    --code-bg: #f5f2ee;
    --ok: #2f6b45;
  }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    :root {
      --bg: #161513;
      --surface: #1e1d1a;
      --border: #33302b;
      --text: #ece8e2;
      --muted: #a09990;
      --accent: #e8834a;
      --accent-soft: #2a1d14;
      --code-bg: #131210;
      --ok: #7bbd93;
    }
  }
  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  body {
    margin: 0;
    background: var(--bg);
    color: var(--text);
    font: 16px/1.65 ui-sans-serif, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Inter, system-ui, sans-serif;
    -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
  }
  .wrap { max-width: 860px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 24px; }
  header { padding: 72px 0 40px; }
  .logo {
    font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -0.02em; font-size: 15px;
    text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--accent); margin-bottom: 28px;
  }
  h1 {
    font-size: clamp(32px, 6vw, 52px); line-height: 1.08;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em; margin: 0 0 20px; font-weight: 700;
  }
  .lede { font-size: clamp(17px, 2.4vw, 20px); color: var(--muted); max-width: 62ch; margin: 0 0 32px; }
  h2 { font-size: 17px; margin: 28px 0 8px; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
  h3 {
    font-size: 13px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.09em;
    color: var(--muted); font-weight: 600; margin: 64px 0 20px;
    padding-bottom: 10px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  p { margin: 0 0 16px; }
  a { color: var(--accent); }
  code {
    font-family: ui-monospace, "SF Mono", Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
    font-size: 0.88em; background: var(--code-bg);
    padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px;
  }
  pre {
    background: var(--code-bg); border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 10px; padding: 18px 20px; overflow-x: auto;
    font-family: ui-monospace, "SF Mono", Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
    font-size: 13.5px; line-height: 1.6; margin: 0 0 20px;
  }
  pre code { background: none; padding: 0; font-size: inherit; }
  .step {
    display: flex; gap: 16px; align-items: baseline;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
  .step-n {
    flex: none; width: 26px; height: 26px; border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--accent-soft); color: var(--accent);
    display: grid; place-items: center; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 700;
    position: relative; top: 4px;
  }
  .cards { display: grid; gap: 14px; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(220px, 1fr)); margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .card {
    background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 12px; padding: 20px;
  }
  .card .big { font-size: 27px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -0.02em; display: block; }
  .card .label { font-size: 13px; color: var(--muted); }
  .table-scroll { overflow-x: auto; margin-bottom: 20px; }
  table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; font-size: 14.5px; min-width: 480px; }
  th, td { text-align: left; padding: 11px 14px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
  th { font-size: 12px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.06em; color: var(--muted); font-weight: 600; }
  td code { white-space: nowrap; }
  .num { text-align: right; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; white-space: nowrap; }
  .note {
    border-left: 3px solid var(--accent); background: var(--accent-soft);
    padding: 14px 18px; border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0; margin: 0 0 20px;
    font-size: 15px;
  }
  .note strong { color: var(--accent); }
  ul { margin: 0 0 16px; padding-left: 22px; }
  li { margin-bottom: 6px; }
  footer {
    margin-top: 72px; padding: 28px 0 56px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border); color: var(--muted); font-size: 14px;
  }

  /* --- audience-led sections ------------------------------------------- */
  /* The base h2/h3 rules in this sheet carry visual roles rather than
     hierarchy, so section and card headings name their look explicitly.
     That keeps the document outline correct without restyling the sheet. */
  .section-label{font-size:13px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.09em;
    color:var(--muted);font-weight:600;margin:56px 0 18px;padding-bottom:10px;
    border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)}
  .card-title{font-size:16.5px;text-transform:none;letter-spacing:-.01em;
    color:var(--text);font-weight:700;margin:0 0 6px;padding:0;border:none}
  .sub-label{font-size:17px;text-transform:none;letter-spacing:-.01em;
    color:var(--text);font-weight:700;margin:30px 0 10px;padding:0;border:none}
  .hero-cta{display:flex;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;margin:0 0 14px}
  .btn{display:inline-block;padding:13px 22px;border-radius:9px;font-weight:600;
       text-decoration:none;font-size:15.5px;border:1px solid transparent}
  .btn-primary{background:var(--accent);color:#fff}
  .btn-primary:hover{filter:brightness(1.07)}
  .btn-ghost{border-color:var(--border);color:var(--text);background:var(--surface)}
  .btn-ghost:hover{border-color:var(--accent);color:var(--accent)}
  .cta-note{font-size:13.5px;color:var(--faint)}
  .who{display:grid;gap:14px;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(230px,1fr))}
  .who .card p{margin:0;font-size:14.5px;color:var(--muted)}
  .who .card .tag{display:inline-block;font-size:11px;text-transform:uppercase;
    letter-spacing:.07em;font-weight:700;color:var(--accent);margin-bottom:9px}
  .does{display:grid;gap:0;margin-bottom:18px}
  .does .item{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(180px,1fr) 2fr;gap:18px;
    padding:15px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);align-items:baseline}
  .does .item:last-child{border-bottom:none}
  .does .item strong{font-size:15.5px}
  .does .item span{color:var(--muted);font-size:14.5px}
  @media (max-width:620px){.does .item{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:4px}}
  .bundle-grid{display:grid;gap:12px;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(190px,1fr));
    margin-bottom:14px}
  .bundle-card{background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:12px;
    padding:20px;position:relative}
  .bundle-card.best{border-color:var(--accent)}
  .bundle-card .amt{font-size:27px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.02em;display:block}
  .bundle-card .qty{font-size:14px;color:var(--text);margin-top:4px;display:block}
  .bundle-card .rate{font-size:12.5px;color:var(--faint);margin-top:8px;display:block}
  .bundle-card .flag{position:absolute;top:-9px;right:14px;background:var(--accent);color:#fff;
    font-size:10.5px;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em;
    padding:3px 9px;border-radius:99px}
  .dev{border-top:1px solid var(--border);margin-top:56px;padding-top:8px}
  .quiet{color:var(--muted);font-size:14.5px}
<%= CsuiteFinderWeb.Nav.css() %></style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="wrap">

<%= CsuiteFinderWeb.Nav.render(nil) %>

<header>
  <h1>Reach the decision-maker, not the contact form.</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    You know the person you need — a VP of Engineering, a founder, a Head of Procurement.
    CSuiteFinder turns their name and their company into a verified work email address,
    so your message lands in an inbox instead of a support queue.
  </p>
  <div class="hero-cta">
    <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/start">Get started — <%= @trial_tokens %> free lookups</a>
    <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="#developers">Read the API docs</a>
  </div>
  <p class="cta-note">No card, no call, no demo. Your first <%= @trial_tokens %> lookups are on us.</p>
</header>

<h2 class="section-label">Who it's for</h2>

<div class="who">
  <div class="card">
    <span class="tag">Sales</span>
    <h3 class="card-title">Get past the gatekeeper</h3>
    <p>
      Start from a company or from a list of names — either way you end up with deliverable
      addresses. Pull the executives at an account, or turn names you already have into
      inboxes, and verify each one before you send so bounces never touch your reputation.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="card">
    <span class="tag">Founders</span>
    <h3 class="card-title">Reach investors and first customers</h3>
    <p>
      Warm intros run out. When you need to reach a partner at a fund, a design partner or
      an early hire directly, you usually have the name and the company and nothing else.
      That's exactly the gap this fills.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="card">
    <span class="tag">Developers</span>
    <h3 class="card-title">One endpoint, one token</h3>
    <p>
      A plain JSON API with no SDK to install and no seat licence. Register with a
      <code>POST</code> and you have a key. <a href="#developers">Jump to the docs →</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</div>

<h2 class="section-label">How it works</h2>

<div class="step"><span class="step-n">1</span><div><strong>Tell us who.</strong> A full name and the company's domain — <em>Jensen Huang</em> at <em>nvidia.com</em>. That's the whole input.</div></div>
<div class="step"><span class="step-n">2</span><div><strong>Get the address.</strong> We work out how that company formats its email and build the person's address from it.</div></div>
<div class="step"><span class="step-n">3</span><div><strong>Check before you send.</strong> Confirm the mailbox is real and deliverable, and see who and what is behind it — all included, no extra charge.</div></div>

<div class="note" style="margin-top:22px">
  <strong>Don't have names yet?</strong> Give us just the company domain and we'll return the
  people at it — filter to <code>executive</code> and you have the C-suite, with addresses and
  job titles. Bring a name and we'll find one address; bring a domain and we'll find the room.
</div>

<h2 class="section-label">What you can do</h2>

<div class="does">
  <div class="item"><strong>Find the people at a company</strong><span>A domain in, named people out — with titles, departments and addresses. Filter to executives for the C-suite.</span></div>
  <div class="item"><strong>Find an email</strong><span>A name and a company domain become a work email address.</span></div>
  <div class="item"><strong>Check it's deliverable</strong><span>Confirm the mailbox is real before you send, so bounces don't hurt your sender reputation.</span></div>
  <div class="item"><strong>Identify an address</strong><span>Given an email, find out whose it is — name, job title, employer.</span></div>
  <div class="item"><strong>Learn a company's format</strong><span>See how a company builds its addresses, and apply it to anyone else there.</span></div>
  <div class="item"><strong>Look up the company</strong><span>Industry, headcount, founding year and location behind any work address.</span></div>
</div>

<h2 class="section-label" id="pricing">Pricing</h2>

<p class="quiet" style="margin-top:-6px">
  You pay for emails — <strong>one token each</strong>, whether you resolve one from a name or
  discover a roomful from a domain. Deliverability checks, identity lookups, company data and
  email formats are all included with any balance. A lookup that finds nothing is free.
</p>

<div class="bundle-grid">
  <%= for b <- @bundles do %>
  <div class="bundle-card<%= if b.best_value, do: " best" %>">
    <%= if b.best_value do %><span class="flag">Better rate</span><% end %>
    <span class="amt">$<%= b.usd %></span>
    <span class="qty"><%= b.tokens %> tokens</span>
    <span class="rate">$<%= b.rate %> per email found · <%= b.finds %> lookups</span>
  </div>
  <% end %>
</div>

<p class="quiet">
  Tokens never expire. Bundles start at $<%= @min_bundle %> and are paid through PayPal.
  Start with <strong><%= @trial_tokens %> free tokens</strong> (<%= @trial_usd %>) to try it
  properly first — that's <%= @trial_tokens %> real lookups, not a preview.
</p>

<p style="margin-top:22px">
  <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/account">Create your free account</a>
</p>

<h2 class="section-label">Why the addresses are good</h2>

<p class="quiet">
  Most companies build every employee's address the same way. We work out that format once and
  apply it — which is why a lookup costs a fraction of a cent instead of the several cents a
  per-person database charges, and why the second person you look up at a company is usually
  instant.
</p>
<p class="quiet">
  Every address can then be verified against the live mailbox before you use it. Checking is
  included, and it is the single best thing you can do for your domain's deliverability:
  a bounced cold email costs you far more than the lookup did.
</p>

<h2 class="section-label">Using it with an AI agent</h2>

<p class="quiet">
  The fastest way in — <a href="/start"><strong>the full walkthrough is here</strong></a>.
  If you work with Claude, ChatGPT, Cursor or any coding agent, you do not have to
  explain this API to it. Point it at our
  <a href="/llms.txt"><code>llms.txt</code></a> and it will know every endpoint,
  parameter and price — the file is generated from the live service, so what it
  reads is what you are charged.
</p>

<p class="quiet"><strong>Paste this to your agent:</strong></p>

<pre><code>Read <%= @base_url %>/llms.txt and use the CSuiteFinder API.
Register for a key, then find the work email for each person in my list.
Verify every address before you give it to me.</code></pre>

<p class="quiet">
  It will register itself, get <%= @trial_tokens %> free lookups and start working. If your
  agent supports remembering instructions, drop the same URL into its project rules
  or <code>AGENTS.md</code> and it will keep the API available for later.
</p>

<div class="note">
  <strong>One thing worth telling your agent:</strong> this finds the address of someone
  you can name — it is not a prospect database and will not build your list. Agents that
  assume otherwise waste turns hunting for a search endpoint that does not exist. The
  <code>llms.txt</code> says so plainly, which is most of why it is worth pointing at.
</div>

<!-- ── developers ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
<div class="dev" id="developers">
<h2 class="section-label">For developers</h2>

<p class="quiet">
  A JSON API over HTTPS. No SDK, no seat licence. Register and you have a key:
</p>

<pre><code>curl -X POST <%= @base_url %>/csuitefinder/register \
  -H 'content-type: application/json' \
  -d '{"email": "you@company.com"}'</code></pre>

<p class="quiet">
  Send the key as <code>Authorization: Bearer &lt;key&gt;</code> on every request. Prefer a
  browser? <a href="/account">Your account page</a> does the same thing, plus balance and billing.
</p>

<h3 class="sub-label">Endpoints</h3>

<div class="table-scroll">
<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Method</th><th>Path</th><th>Parameters</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>POST</td><td><code>/csuitefinder/email/find</code></td><td><code>full_name</code>, <code>domain</code>, <code>email</code><span class="label"> (optional)</span></td></tr>
    <tr><td>POST</td><td><code>/csuitefinder/email/deliverable</code></td><td><code>email</code></td></tr>
    <tr><td>POST</td><td><code>/csuitefinder/email/enrich</code></td><td><code>email</code></td></tr>
    <tr><td>POST</td><td><code>/csuitefinder/email/pattern</code></td><td><code>email</code></td></tr>
    <tr><td>POST</td><td><code>/csuitefinder/name/who</code></td><td><code>email</code></td></tr>
    <tr><td>POST</td><td><code>/csuitefinder/company/people</code></td><td><code>domain</code>, <code>department</code>, <code>limit</code> — who works there</td></tr>
    <tr><td>POST</td><td><code>/csuitefinder/company/find</code></td><td><code>email</code> — which company this is</td></tr>
    <tr><td>POST</td><td><code>/csuitefinder/company/info</code></td><td><code>email</code> or <code>domain</code> — the full profile</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
</div>

<p class="quiet">
  Every endpoint also accepts <code>GET</code> with a query string, and <code>refresh=true</code>
  to force a re-check. The optional <code>email</code> on <code>/email/find</code> is a
  colleague's address at the same company: give us one address there and we can resolve the rest.
</p>

<h3 class="sub-label">Example</h3>

<pre><code>curl -H "Authorization: Bearer $CSF_KEY" \
  "<%= @base_url %>/csuitefinder/email/find?full_name=Jensen%20Huang&domain=nvidia.com"

{
  "email": "jhuang@nvidia.com",
  "full_name": "Jensen Huang",
  "domain": "nvidia.com",
  "found": true,
  "confidence": 0.937638
}</code></pre>

<h3 class="sub-label">Per-endpoint cost</h3>

<div class="table-scroll">
<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Endpoint</th><th class="num">Tokens</th><th class="num">Effective</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <%= for {endpoint, tokens, usd} <- @price_rows do %>
    <tr>
      <td><code><%= endpoint %></code></td>
      <td class="num"><%= if tokens > 0, do: tokens, else: "—" %></td>
      <td class="num"><%= if tokens > 0, do: "$" <> usd, else: "included" %></td>
    </tr>
    <% end %>
  </tbody>
</table>
</div>

<h3 class="sub-label">Managing your account</h3>

<div class="table-scroll">
<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Path</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td><code>GET /csuitefinder/billing/balance</code></td><td>Token balance and the full price list</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>GET /csuitefinder/billing/usage?days=30</code></td><td>Calls, cache hits and tokens spent per endpoint</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>GET /csuitefinder/keys</code></td><td>Your API keys — mint a spare, revoke an old one</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>POST /csuitefinder/billing/topup</code></td><td>Buy a bundle — returns a PayPal approval link</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>GET /csuitefinder/health</code></td><td>Service status</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>

<footer>
  <a href="/start">Get started</a> ·
  <a href="/account">Your account</a> ·
  <a href="/llms.txt">llms.txt</a> ·
  <a href="/csuitefinder/pricing">pricing as JSON</a> ·
  <a href="/csuitefinder/health">status</a>
</footer>

</div>
</body>
</html>
